---
import Callout from "~/components/illustration-kit/Callout.astro"
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import Panel from "~/components/illustration-kit/Panel.astro"
import SideBySide from "~/components/illustration-kit/SideBySide.astro"
---

<IllustrationFigure lead="Which fraud detector gets the higher accuracy score?">
  <p class="text-base leading-normal">
    Imagine 100 payments. <strong>Just one is fraudulent.</strong> Both detectors examine the
    same payments.
  </p>

  <SideBySide>
    <Panel title="A. Says all are legitimate">
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm">Accuracy</p>
      <p class="text-3xl font-bold">99%</p>
      <div class="mt-4 border-t-2 border-ink pt-3">
        <p class="text-sm">Frauds found</p>
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-series-red">0 of 1</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-normal">Misses the fraud entirely.</p>
      </div>
    </Panel>
    <Panel title="B. Flags 3 payments">
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm">Accuracy</p>
      <p class="text-3xl font-bold">98%</p>
      <div class="mt-4 border-t-2 border-ink pt-3">
        <p class="text-sm">Frauds found</p>
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-series-green">1 of 1</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-normal">Finds the fraud, with 2 false alarms.</p>
      </div>
    </Panel>
  </SideBySide>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p class="leading-normal">
      <strong>A scores higher, yet finds no fraud.</strong> Its 99 correct answers are all
      legitimate payments. B makes two mistakes but catches the only fraud.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <Fragment slot="caption">
    If finding fraud matters, accuracy alone gives the wrong impression. Which detector is
    more useful also depends on the cost of false alarms.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
